WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.617
The next bridge is bind tools.

00:00:02.617 --> 00:00:08.282
Binding tools tells the chat model which approved tool schemas exist.

00:00:08.282 --> 00:00:14.282
The model can then request one of those tools if its integration supports tool calling.

00:00:14.282 --> 00:00:16.700
But binding is not permission.

00:00:17.211 --> 00:00:21.328
The application still decides whether a requested tool can run.

00:00:21.328 --> 00:00:25.768
It validates arguments. It checks the user's authorization.

00:00:25.768 --> 00:00:28.148
It handles retries and errors.

00:00:28.148 --> 00:00:34.243
It controls side effects. For example, a model might request an order lookup.

00:00:34.243 --> 00:00:39.037
Your code should still verify that the current user is allowed to access that order.

00:00:39.675 --> 00:00:42.787
Think of bind tools as showing the model the menu.

00:00:42.787 --> 00:00:48.128
The application is still the security guard, the cashier, and the execution engine.
